{
  "suite": "cold-restarts",
  "target": "tryaii.claude_code.sessions.cold_restarts (SDK, imported calls) and the server's mark_cold_restarts (live events)",
  "description": "Synthetic calls (no real data) pinning the Claude Code cold cache restart rule. Within one session's main-thread calls in time order (process 'main'; every other process is a subagent and is excluded): the first main call is never cold; a call is cold when the gap since the previous main call of the same session is more than gap_minutes AND usage.cache_write_tokens >= max(min_write_tokens, usage.cached_tokens). ttl: the call's own cache_writes split ('1h' when the 1h part is larger, '5m' when only 5m is set); without a split the session's last split, else default_ttl. reason: 'expired' when gap >= ttl, else 'model_switch' when the model differs from the previous main call's, else 'other'. cost_usd = 5m part x (1.25 x input - cache read) + 1h part x (2 x input - cache read), with the prices below (synthetic, per million tokens), rounded to 6 dp; a write without a 5m/1h split is priced whole at the call's resolved ttl. default_ttl is passed explicitly: the SDK's default for imported calls is 5m, while the server defaults live main-thread calls to 1h, so its test must pass rule.default_ttl (every no-split cold call here resolves to 5m). cache_cold is null for subagent calls. Sessions are named only by ordinal of their first main call.",
  "rule": {
    "gap_minutes": 5,
    "min_write_tokens": 1024,
    "default_ttl": "5m",
    "ttl_minutes": {
      "5m": 5,
      "1h": 60
    },
    "reasons": [
      "expired",
      "model_switch",
      "other"
    ],
    "cache_write_factors": {
      "5m": 1.25,
      "1h": 2.0
    }
  },
  "prices": {
